24	//   'self'  — the task touches only its own repo; a project-only executor session
25	//             is all it needs. This is the default, and almost every task's scope.
26	//   'fleet' — the task reaches across the owner's other repos (e.g. growth-promote
27	//             reads every member's local packs), so its dispatch goes to a
28	//             SEPARATE, broader-scoped executor. Isolating this to the few tasks
29	//             that truly need it keeps the fleet-wide session grant off every
30	//             ordinary project's executor. The scheduler routes a fleet task's
31	//             dispatch to the `ready-for-agent-fleet` label so a distinct executor
32	//             routine (with the owner's repos in its sources) runs it.
